<article class="env-lemma" id="0GMN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GMN">Lemma <span data-tag="0GMN">4.23.3</span>.</a> Let $F : \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ be a functor. Suppose all finite colimits exist in $\mathcal{A}$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/002Q" data-tag="002Q">4.18.7</a>. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$F$ is right exact, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$F$ commutes with finite coproducts and coequalizers, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$F$ transforms an initial object of $\mathcal{A}$ into an initial object of $\mathcal{B}$, and commutes with pushouts. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Dual to Lemma <a href="/tag/0035" data-tag="0035">4.23.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>